[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2455729289","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98826#issuecomment-2455729289","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98826","id":2455729289,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6SX3SJ","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-04T21:22:58Z","updated_at":"2024-11-04T21:22:58Z","body":"@TokageItLab, does anyone remember what this is? \r\n\r\nI am satisfied with merging this once we know the reason or someone can prove the new code does the same thing as the existing code.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2455729289/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2455794017","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98826#issuecomment-2455794017","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98826","id":2455794017,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6SYHFh","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-04T22:04:29Z","updated_at":"2024-11-05T12:09:51Z","body":"As far as I remember, the original problem was that the FPS mode values were not restored correctly by lacking precision when serialized to `.tres` and `.tscn`.\r\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/92670\r\n- issue by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/92273\r\n\r\nAs for `modf()`, it was implemented follow for snapping when using values above 1s:\r\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/96328\r\n- issue by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/96159\r\n\r\nUp until this point, only int values have been allowed for FPS, but a PR is sent to allow float FPS.\r\n\r\nThe 0.0625 snap is due to the fix in:\r\n-  https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/97569\r\n  - issue by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/97548\r\n\r\nThen, two approaches are mixed here, which might cause some confusion.\r\n\r\nSo finally, I think this PR would be okay if the following test results are correct:\r\n\r\n- [ ] Save `.tres` and `.tscn` in FPS mode and restart Godot, the snap values is restored correctly\r\n- [ ] Save `.tres` and `.tscn` in Second mode and restart Godot, the snap value is restored correctly\r\n- [ ] In Second mode, equal or greater than 1.0s snap value is working correctly\r\n- [ ] In Second mode, less than 1.0s snap value is working correctly\r\n- [ ] In FPS mode, integer FPS snap value is working correctly\r\n- [ ] In FPS mode, float FPS snap value is working correctly\r\n- [ ] When switching between Second mode and FPS mode with a snap value of 1.0s or less, the snap value is not corrupted (Do not internally snap to a value less than 0.0625)\r\n- [ ] When switching between Second mode and FPS mode with a snap value of larget than 1.0s, the snap value is not corrupted ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2455794017/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2457443555","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98826#issuecomment-2457443555","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98826","id":2457443555,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6SeZzj","user":{"login":"UnfavorableEnhancer","id":100960666,"node_id":"U_kgDOBgSJmg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100960666?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/UnfavorableEnhancer","html_url":"https://github.com/UnfavorableEnhancer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UnfavorableEnhancer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UnfavorableEnhancer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UnfavorableEnhancer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UnfavorableEnhancer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UnfavorableEnhancer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UnfavorableEnhancer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UnfavorableEnhancer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UnfavorableEnhancer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UnfavorableEnhancer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-05T15:15:55Z","updated_at":"2024-11-05T15:50:19Z","body":"> As I described in [#98609 (comment)](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98609#issuecomment-2456985645), probably this fix should only be applied when the snapping value is 1.0s or greater. Also, I think we need to document snaps less than 1.0 (although we can separate the documentation PR from this IMO).\r\n> \r\n> @fire @lyuma Should glTF baking on import also take into account the 1.0s interval?\r\n\r\nI don't really like idea of ignoring values below 1.0s. Code which was before equally breaked snap values both above 1.0s and below 1.0s (Quoting myself: The same rules apply for any integer value like 2.225 is snapped to 2.25, or 4.3 is snapped to 4.33333...).\r\nAnd I think that rounding snap values at all is a bad practice, since sometimes you need a precise snap value to make your animation correctly (for example my game uses a lot of music BPM tied animations, so I quite oftenly use quite precise float values like 0.432 or 5.393 to sync animation keys to the music), and overall game engine should allow for any possibilities, not limit them.\r\n\r\n> So finally, I think this PR would be okay if the following test results are correct:\r\n> \r\n> * [ ]  Save `.tres` and `.tscn` in FPS mode and restart Godot, the snap values is restored correctly\r\n> * [ ]  Save `.tres` and `.tscn` in Second mode and restart Godot, the snap value is restored correctly\r\n> * [ ]  In Second mode, equal or greater than 1.0s snap value is working correctly\r\n> * [ ]  In Second mode, less than 1.0s snap value is working correctly\r\n> * [ ]  In FPS mode, integer FPS snap value is working correctly\r\n> * [ ]  In FPS mode, float FPS snap value is working correctly\r\n> * [ ]  When switching between Second mode and FPS mode with a snap value of 1.0s or less, the snap value is not corrupted (Do not internally snap to a value less than 0.0625)\r\n> * [ ]  When switching between Second mode and FPS mode with a snap value of larget than 1.0s, the snap value is not corrupted\r\n\r\nAlso tested those things and everything worked except last 4 tests, but tbh I'm not sure how FPS mode should work at all, so I'm still investigating that.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2457443555/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2457598834","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98826#issuecomment-2457598834","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98826","id":2457598834,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Se_ty","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-05T16:11:42Z","updated_at":"2024-11-05T16:19:13Z","body":"I understand that some people need precise snapping for music, but there are users who want to use Second mode while prioritizing FPS for animation to check the current second time while making frame animations.\r\n\r\nTherefore, I think that for the most compatible and safe solution, we need to add FPS compatible mode as an option for Second mode, as in Approach 3 described there https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98609#issuecomment-2456985645.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2457598834/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2457797127","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98826#issuecomment-2457797127","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98826","id":2457797127,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6SfwIH","user":{"login":"UnfavorableEnhancer","id":100960666,"node_id":"U_kgDOBgSJmg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100960666?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/UnfavorableEnhancer","html_url":"https://github.com/UnfavorableEnhancer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UnfavorableEnhancer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UnfavorableEnhancer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UnfavorableEnhancer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UnfavorableEnhancer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UnfavorableEnhancer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UnfavorableEnhancer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UnfavorableEnhancer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UnfavorableEnhancer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UnfavorableEnhancer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-05T17:39:15Z","updated_at":"2024-11-05T17:39:15Z","body":"just did little fix for this PR\r\nI've realized that adding \"snapped\" functions was actually a bad idea, it introduced some accumulation issues in fps mode and it also snapped to incorrect values\r\nso I've checked everything and all is working fine now, but accumulation error still occur when you work in seconds mode, so adding a special toggle for fixing it, is actually a good idea, but I kinda think that it might be out of scope of this PR\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2457797127/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2457807207","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98826#issuecomment-2457807207","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98826","id":2457807207,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Sfyln","user":{"login":"UnfavorableEnhancer","id":100960666,"node_id":"U_kgDOBgSJmg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100960666?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/UnfavorableEnhancer","html_url":"https://github.com/UnfavorableEnhancer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UnfavorableEnhancer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UnfavorableEnhancer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com